{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 60,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Most of us tie our shoe laces wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3000,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two ways to tie\na knot in your shoe laces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6030,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In one, you go counterclockwise\naround the loop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9330,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in the other, you go clockwise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12690,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These two methods look almost identical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15330,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but one of these knots is\nfar superior to the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18240,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't loosen or come\nuntied nearly as easily."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21660,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand why,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22680,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to delve into knot theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26100,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a whole branch of mathematics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28380,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that aims to identify,\ncategorize and understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31240,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every possible knot that could ever exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34950,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far, we have discovered\nthe first 352,152,252 knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41190,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each one has its own"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42270,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particular properties and characteristics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45300,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's fascinating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46860,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there's something\nlike a periodic table"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48870,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for knots out there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50790,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's not pure math."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52920,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory has turned out\nto be remarkably useful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55860,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is core to the structure\nof proteins and DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59220,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's leading to new materials"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61230,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could be stronger than Kevlar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63360,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's even used to develop medicines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65580,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that save millions of lives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68940,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of this just from trying\nto understand the humble knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78030,
    "dDurationMs": 1773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is a knot?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80839,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in our everyday lives,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82380,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see knots like this or this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85950,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you are trying to\nrigorously study knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88980,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want to be able to pull them apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91290,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can really see what's going on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93720,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is knots like\nthis are held together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95910,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only by tension and friction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97740,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you pull on them too hard,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99510,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they fall apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100890,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in order to capture\nthe knot on the rope,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104310,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematicians got the idea\nto connect the two ends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108510,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now, well, you can tease\nthe knot apart to study it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113340,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it will never fundamentally change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116100,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in knot theory, all\nknots exist on closed loops."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119670,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means the simplest knot you can have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121980,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just a circle like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124410,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, admittedly, this\nis not much of a knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126180,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why it is called an unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131250,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here is another knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133050,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, it's made of a single piece of rope"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135150,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that forms a closed loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137160,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here is another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139200,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two knots are only different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140850,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you can't make one into the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142890,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without breaking the loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144690,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the simplest\nknot after the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147420,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is called the trefoil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149280,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can see that there's no way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150570,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for me to turn this back into a circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153210,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unless I actually break it open,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156330,
    "dDurationMs": 3843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take out the knot and\nthen close it up again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161610,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I have two unknots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164010,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is surprisingly hard to\ntell two knots apart by eye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168000,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here is a simple mystery knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170760,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it an unknot, a trefoil or neither?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173820,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll give you a second to figure it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178410,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is in fact a trefoil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180690,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you can see if I just untwist this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183930,
    "dDurationMs": 2523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and rearrange the knot a little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187500,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And our first complicated knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190440,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, it is actually just the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193950,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm going to try to disentangle\nit so you can see that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200220,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There you go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201570,
    "dDurationMs": 3393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was just a single loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205920,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, these are all unknots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209010,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is where the problem begins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211110,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't just randomly tangle some rope"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213630,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and connect the ends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215040,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make a new mathematical knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216540,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to prove"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not just a tangled up\nversion of another knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220560,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do you tell two knots apart?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224310,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This one question,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225360,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also known as the knot\nequivalence problem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227580,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is so famously difficult"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229080,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it's propelled the\nentire field of knot theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231330,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for over 150 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233520,
    "dDurationMs": 2827,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alan Turing even wrote\nin his final publication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236347,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"No systematic method is yet known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238327,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"by which one can tell whether\ntwo knots are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241447,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"A decision problem which\nmight well be unsolvable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243997,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"is the one concerning knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246097,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The results in this\narticle set certain bounds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248407,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"to what we can hope to\nachieve purely by reasoning.\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253830,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Previously, the most famous\nknot problem in history"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256410,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the Gordian knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258090,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was said that whoever untangled\nthis massive knotted rope"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261630,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was destined to rule all of Asia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264600,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Legend goes, Alexander the Great"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266220,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply came along and\nsliced right through it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268890,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would not be a valid\nsolution in knot theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273090,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are other\nfamous knots of history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275640,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The endless knot is seen as far back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277710,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as clay tablets from the Indus Valley,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279630,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was used in\nMedieval Celtic designs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282240,
    "dDurationMs": 2583,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chinese knot work and\nHinduism and Buddhism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286140,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Incan civilization,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287610,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knots were tied on chords called quipu"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289890,
    "dDurationMs": 2913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to track everything\nfrom taxes to calendars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293880,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can even find a knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294920,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the coat of arms for\nthe House of Borromeo,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297480,
    "dDurationMs": 3729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an Italian noble family that\nhas existed since the 1300s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301209,
    "dDurationMs": 2811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Borromeon rings\nare technically a link,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304020,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is just a knot with\nmultiple loops of rope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307620,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most basic link is the unlink,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310260,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two loops which aren't actually connected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312270,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much like the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314190,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After that is the Hopf link."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316410,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then later, the Borromeon rings and more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319830,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the knot equivalence problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321330,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was only encountered centuries later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327270,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In January of 1867,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329340,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scottish physicist Peter Guthrie Tait"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331860,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "showed off his homemade smoke machine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333510,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to renowned scientist William Thomson,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335610,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "later Lord Kelvin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337440,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait had read a paper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338460,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that said a vortex ring\nshould be eternally stable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341820,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in an ideal fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343860,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So intrigued, he set up two wooden boxes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346410,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "containing a kind of toxic mixture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348720,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of ammonia, sulfuric acid and salt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352110,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When he tapped a towel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353190,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stretched across the back of each box,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355320,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chemical smoke popped\nout of a circular cutout"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358410,
    "dDurationMs": 1592,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in perfect rings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360002,
    "dDurationMs": 3538,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kelvin, watching, was\ntransfixed by the rings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363540,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had been pondering\nthe composition of atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366330,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a fundamental question of the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368490,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and suddenly he saw an answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370920,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He declared that atoms must be made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373050,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of vortex rings of ether,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375570,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an invisible everywhere medium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378150,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Different knots of vortex rings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379980,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would make different elements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381660,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The shape of the Hopf link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383070,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explained the double\nspectral lines of sodium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385410,
    "dDurationMs": 2553,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The simple unknot ring was hydrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389610,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait was skeptical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391170,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as Kelvin's vortex model of the atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393150,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "became a leading theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394890,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait began investigating knots in earnest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397590,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his mind,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398423,
    "dDurationMs": 2137,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creating a periodic table of the elements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400560,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with every new knot he found."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402900,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The crossing number is an\neasy way to categorize knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406050,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just take the simplest form of a knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408210,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one with no extra twists or tangles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410970,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and count up all its crossings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413640,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By hand, Tait discovered a three\ncrossing knot, the trefoil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417420,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then a four crossing\nknot, the figure eight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then two five crossing knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421920,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three six crossing knots and\nseven seven crossing knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426300,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One quick note, knots are additive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428850,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can stick multiple knots\ntogether to make a new knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431670,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like combining these two trefoils\ninto a six crossing knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435150,
    "dDurationMs": 1975,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called a composite knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437125,
    "dDurationMs": 3695,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but some knots aren't\ndecomposable into simpler knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440820,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are known as prime knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443280,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since all composite knots\nare just built from primes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446130,
    "dDurationMs": 2973,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people mainly focus on\ntabulating prime knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451770,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately for Tait,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453390,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "warning signs were on the horizon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454950,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for Lord Kelvin's vortex\ntheory of the atom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457350,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mendeleev's first periodic table\nhad been published in 1869."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461190,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Michelson-Morley\nexperiment sowed seeds of doubt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463740,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about an ether in 1887,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465780,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the most damning result"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467190,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was JJ Thomson's discovery\nof the electron in 1897."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471330,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there were particles\nsmaller than the atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474000,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which were inside atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475960,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Tait was already in too\ndeep with knots to stop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479670,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had even roped in his academic rival"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482220,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and close friend James Clerk Maxwell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484530,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Maxwell's equations fame."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486780,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Tait's influence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488130,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maxwell became a knot enthusiast\nfor the rest of his life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491880,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His last poem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493200,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "written shortly before his\ndeath from stomach cancer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495930,
    "dDurationMs": 3787,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even begins, \"My soul's\nan amphichiral knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499717,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"upon a liquid vortex wrought.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505590,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Assisted in part by hundreds\nof letters with Maxwell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508470,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait published his list"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509550,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of knots up to seven crossings in 1877,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512970,
    "dDurationMs": 3213,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first math paper with\nthe word knots in its title."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517050,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then Tait paused his\nsearch for seven years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520020,
    "dDurationMs": 1147,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a speech, he stated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521167,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"The requisite labor increases\nwith extreme rapidity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524227,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"as the number of crossings is increased."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526537,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Someone with the requisite leisure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528097,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"should try to extend this list,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529837,
    "dDurationMs": 2843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"if possible, up to 11.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532680,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two mathematicians took him\nup on his call for help,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535620,
    "dDurationMs": 2103,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thomas Kirkman and Charles Little."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538955,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Together, the three of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540155,
    "dDurationMs": 3205,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were able to find all\n21 eight crossing knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543360,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all 49 nine crossing knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545490,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all 166 10 crossing knots by 1899,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549719,
    "dDurationMs": 2851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just two years before Tait's death."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552570,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was all done painstakingly by hand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555750,
    "dDurationMs": 1597,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait admits in his paper,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557347,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I cannot be absolutely certain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559777,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all those groups are\nessentially different,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561907,
    "dDurationMs": 1793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one from another.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563700,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the process of tabulating knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565530,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he had uncovered the central problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568140,
    "dDurationMs": 1773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how to possibly tell them apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572430,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Somewhat miraculously,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573930,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tait, Kirkman and Little\nhad done a near perfect job"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576810,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with their knot tables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578070,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their list stood for 75\nyears without change,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581280,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until a single correction in 1973."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584250,
    "dDurationMs": 1623,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But more on that later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587490,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For decades after Tait's death,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589320,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little progress was made on\nthe knot equivalence problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592650,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1927,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593850,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "German mathematician Kurt Reidemeister"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595950,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proved a radical theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598080,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You only need three types of moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599910,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to transform any two identical\nknots into each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603630,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The twist, the poke and the slide,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607140,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you move a string"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608130,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from one side of a crossing to the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610650,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we can prove some knots are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613470,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you can show that they're connected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614760,
    "dDurationMs": 1413,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Reidemeister moves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621240,
    "dDurationMs": 2343,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you've proven that they must be identical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625590,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we still don't know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626850,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how to prove any knots\ndifferent from each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629700,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you could do Reidemeister moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631530,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on one knot for centuries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632820,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without it ever looking\nlike the other knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635490,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And maybe they're actually different,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637440,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but maybe they're the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638850,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you just never made the right move"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640740,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to show that that is true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642600,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This may have been where\nTuring was coming from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644790,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he called the knot\nequivalence problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647280,
    "dDurationMs": 1803,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "potentially undecidable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650070,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1961,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653190,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematician Wolfgang Haken\ncreated a computer algorithm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656580,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that solved the not equivalence\nproblem definitively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660150,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for this specific case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661290,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of distinguishing any\nknot from the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664470,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That said, his paper\nwas over 130 pages long"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668430,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the algorithm would've taken longer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670380,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the age of the universe\nto run for large knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674160,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2001, building on Haken's work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676560,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematicians found a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677640,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to distinguish between\nany knot and the unknot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680250,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by simply setting an upper bound"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681990,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the number of Reidemeister\nmoves needed to connect them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685290,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you check all sequences\nof Reidemeister moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687630,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to that number,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688710,
    "dDurationMs": 3183,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can prove if the knot\nis the unknot or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694530,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's just one problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696060,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That upper bound was two\nto the 100 billion n moves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701280,
    "dDurationMs": 870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As of today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702150,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the upper bound has improved dramatically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704160,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to just 236 n to the power of 11."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708510,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, while smaller than before,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710220,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "checking all possible\nsequences of Reidemeister moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713130,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to this number is still unfathomable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716400,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a single crossing knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718520,
    "dDurationMs": 2282,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is larger than the number of stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720802,
    "dDurationMs": 2141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the observable universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724680,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2011, mathematicians\nfound an upper bound"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727110,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the number of Reidemeister moves needed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728850,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to connect any two knots or links,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731490,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solving the entire knot\nequivalence problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735630,
    "dDurationMs": 1923,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the upper bound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739020,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, raise two to the second power,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741780,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then raise that to the power of two again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744090,
    "dDurationMs": 3813,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This operation is called\ntetration, and it grows fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749042,
    "dDurationMs": 3508,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now keep doing it until you\nhave raised two to itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752550,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 to the million n times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756120,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cap it off with n again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758820,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is easily the largest number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760770,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have ever shown in a video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763290,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even just to have a\nsolution is remarkable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766200,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given that Turing thought the problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767670,
    "dDurationMs": 3423,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was potentially undecidable\nonly 60 years earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772101,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it's this hard to tell two knots apart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775890,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how have we managed to tabulate\n350 million different knots?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781440,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, there are some properties of a knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783240,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that never change,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784260,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no matter how much you\ntwist or tangle it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787440,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are called invariants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789390,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these invariants will\nbe different for some knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792450,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compared to other ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793710,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can use them as\nhallmarks of a particular knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797190,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're not perfectly discriminating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799290,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, some knots will share invariants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801900,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if two knots have different invariants"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803910,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you know for sure\nthat they are different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807000,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Crossing number is itself aninvariant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809520,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two knots can't be identical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they have different crossing numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813720,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the crossing number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814740,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is surprisingly difficult to calculate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817140,
    "dDurationMs": 2305,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can put extra crossings into any knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819445,
    "dDurationMs": 2855,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like just throw in a bunch of twists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822300,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Different variations of the same knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824400,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are known as different\nprojections of that knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827940,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Crossing number measures the\nleast number of crossings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830940,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a knot can have,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832230,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it only works for the\nsimplest projection of a knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835170,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also known as its reduced form,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837780,
    "dDurationMs": 3465,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's difficult to ensure\nthat a knot is fully reduced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841245,
    "dDurationMs": 2565,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, we can use another invariant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843810,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one that's true right away\nfor all projections of a knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846900,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it'll give the same value"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848670,
    "dDurationMs": 3843,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both for a messy trefoil\nand for a reduced trefoil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853530,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This first invariant is tricolorability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856350,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or whether or knot can be\ncolored in with three colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860220,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take a diagram of a knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861750,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and color in each individual segment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864540,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are just separated\nby under crossings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867240,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you would lift\nyour pen off the page."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869730,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tricolorability only has two rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872520,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, you must use at least two colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875130,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you can color any\nknot in with one color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878340,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And second, at crossings,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880320,
    "dDurationMs": 1248,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the three intersecting strands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881568,
    "dDurationMs": 4152,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must either be all the same\ncolor or all different colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885720,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically no two colored crossings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889050,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are just two\ncategories of this invariant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891300,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "either a knot is tricolorable or it's not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894450,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Identical knots must match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896100,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if one knot is tricolorable\nand the other one isn't,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898980,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you know they're different knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901710,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's hard to believe that\ntricolorability is constant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904530,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across any possible\nprojection of the same knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907320,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but since you only need Reidemeister moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909360,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to move between projections,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911070,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we just need to prove"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911910,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it isn't affected\nby Reidemeister moves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914700,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The twist is easy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916200,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything's one color already,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917760,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it stays that way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919560,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the poke,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920393,
    "dDurationMs": 2947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the intersection of two colors\nmeans that the loop formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923340,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must become the third color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924930,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we have three colors\nat every intersection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927540,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the slide,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928560,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you never have to break tricolorability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930330,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you start with three\ncolors at three intersections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933300,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then switch one\nintersection to just one color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936870,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So any knot will maintain\nits tricolorability,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no matter what Reidemeister moves you do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942840,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a good time to note"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944580,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we never actually proved\nthe trefoil and the unknot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947640,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were two different knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949410,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we can do it now with tricolorability."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952680,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The unknot is not tricolorable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955410,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since you can't use at least\ntwo colors to color it in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958260,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the trefoil is easily tricolorable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960780,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just color in each of the three\nsegments a different color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964110,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The crossings all have three colors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966000,
    "dDurationMs": 1713,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it is tricolorable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968580,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969420,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every possible projection of\nthe trefoil is tricolorable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972900,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while every possible\nprojection of the unknot isn't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975870,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these two knots must\nbe different knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978930,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This invariant isn't very specific."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981300,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It only gives you two\ncategories across all knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984420,
    "dDurationMs": 1947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the next knot after the trefoil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986367,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the figure eight knot, isn't tricolorable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989310,
    "dDurationMs": 2332,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's always a crossing with two colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991642,
    "dDurationMs": 3488,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do we prove that this\nis different from the unknot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995130,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which also isn't tricolorable?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998190,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tricolorability expands into\na much more powerful invariant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001910,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called p-colorability,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003770,
    "dDurationMs": 3277,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where p can be any prime\nnumber besides two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007047,
    "dDurationMs": 1703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of using colors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008750,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll number each strand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010400,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with integers between\nzero and p minus one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014330,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "p-colorability has two rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016910,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, you must use at\nleast two different numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, at crossings,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1022400,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two bottom strands added\ntogether and divided by p"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026120,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must give the same remainder"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028130,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as twice the top strand divided by p."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032130,
    "dDurationMs": 4131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tricolorability was just\na simple version of this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1036261,
    "dDurationMs": 2609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we go from three to five colorability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038870,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the figure eight knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040100,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can number the strands zero, one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043760,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then this strand must give\na remainder of zero, so four,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048920,
    "dDurationMs": 3693,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this strand must give a\nremainder of two, so three."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053690,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This knot is five colorable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056240,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's not the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058850,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "p-colorability is a huge tool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060980,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The unknot is completely uncolorable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063470,
    "dDurationMs": 3723,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so any knot with any\ncolorability can't be the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068180,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "p-colorability still\ndoesn't cover everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071360,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of the most powerful\ninvariants right now,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073850,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ones that can distinguish\nbetween the most unique knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077030,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are polynomials."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078650,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Alexander polynomial\nwas the first one discovered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081770,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back in 1923 before\neven Reidemeister moves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085730,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like p-colorability,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087290,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it relies on only two rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090260,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that the Alexander\npolynomial of the unknot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093320,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095090,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second is that you can zoom in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097130,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on any single crossing of a knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099380,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and vary it in three possible positions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102320,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forward, backward and separate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105530,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Alexander polynomial\ngives a relationship"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107840,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the three resulting knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110630,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's do an example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112040,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's the Alexander\npolynomial for the unlink?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115250,
    "dDurationMs": 2487,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if we zoom into\nthis separate crossing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117737,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then vary it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119330,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see that the other two knots\nformed are both the unknot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123590,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we can plug in one for both of them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125930,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we get that the Alexander\npolynomial for the unlink"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128570,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130370,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we can do the same for the Hopf link."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132470,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Taking this crossing as\nthe forward crossing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134810,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then seeing that the backward\ncrossing gives us the unlink,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137450,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the separate crossing is the unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139550,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the Alexander polynomial\nfor the Hopf link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142100,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is minus t to the 1/2\nplus t to the minus 1/2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146270,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now we can do the trefoil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147980,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we vary this crossing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149420,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we get that the backward\ncrossing gives us the unknot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1152120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the separate crossing\ngives the Hopf link."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the Alexander polynomial is t minus one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157760,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus t to the negative one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160280,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The polynomial is designed so\nthat we get separate results"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163430,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for as many knots and links as we can,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166400,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is recursive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167930,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can calculate the polynomial forever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169970,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for bigger and bigger knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172760,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Alexander polynomial stood\nunchanged for over 60 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176780,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the knot invariant of choice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178910,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1984,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180350,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was upended by an unlikely discovery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183140,
    "dDurationMs": 1379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mathematician Vaughan Jones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184519,
    "dDurationMs": 2491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had been working on a type of algebra"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187010,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for statistical mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188450,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a concept in physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189830,
    "dDurationMs": 990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when he realized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190820,
    "dDurationMs": 3543,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his work resembled a series\nof equations in knot theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195230,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He traveled to New York"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196400,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to consult knot theorist Joan\nBirman at Columbia University,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200180,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who helped refine his equations\ninto a knot invariant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203780,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They met again a week later"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205070,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tested it against knot diagrams"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1207020,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from Birman's filing cabinet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208790,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quickly realizing Jones had discovered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a brand new polynomial invariant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214520,
    "dDurationMs": 3063,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He scribbled down all their\nwork in a 15 page letter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218810,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Jones polynomial\nis like the Alexander,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221180,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but with the more specific\nequation for the second rule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223880,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that lets it distinguish many more knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226220,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For this discovery,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227660,
    "dDurationMs": 3013,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jones won the field's medal in 1990."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230673,
    "dDurationMs": 2537,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first new polynomial invariant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233210,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kicked up a fervor in knot theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235340,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just months after Joan's result,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237050,
    "dDurationMs": 2122,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "six mathematicians each independently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1239172,
    "dDurationMs": 2678,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found an improved\nversion of his polynomial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1241850,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with two variables instead of one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244520,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The editors of the American Math Society"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246590,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "published all their papers together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248660,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "naming it The HOMFLY polynomial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251060,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two Polish Mathematicians missed the news"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253370,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and discovered it again\na couple months later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255710,
    "dDurationMs": 3563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upon which it became the\nHOMFLY-PT polynomial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260870,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "None of these invariants works alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263330,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just like if you were\nsearching for a person,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265580,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'd start by checking a\nfirst name, then a last name,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268580,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then a birthday and so on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270890,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to eventually narrow your\nsearch down to just one person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274790,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, knots have\ndozens of invariants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278060,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which when taken together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279650,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uniquely identify them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281720,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With invariants to prove\nif knots are different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1284090,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Reidemeister moves to\nprove if knots are the same,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1286940,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can attack from two angles\nto meet the gargantuan task"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290780,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of distinguishing every single knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294470,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this method isn't perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296690,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These two knots were\nlisted next to each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298820,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Tait's knot tables for over 75 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301790,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were the same by\nall invariant accounts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304400,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Tait and Little likely\ntried Reidemeister moves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307250,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see if they could\ntransform one into the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309440,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once they failed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310790,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they listed them as two separate knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313940,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kenneth Perko, a lawyer who\nhad studied knot theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316880,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spotted them in 1973"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318680,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while looking through Little's\ntable of 10 crossing knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321830,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suspicious of their similarities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1323660,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he pulled out a yellow legal pad"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325250,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to sketch some Reidemeister moves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1327140,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he quickly found a way\nto connect the two knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330200,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These two projections now\nknown as the Perko pair"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333410,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the same knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335390,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the knot tables of\nTait, Kirkman and Little"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337940,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were issued their single correction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340160,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And instead of 166 ten crossing knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342950,
    "dDurationMs": 2283,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are 165."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It had taken decades of work\nto tabulate all 249 prime knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350840,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to 10 crossings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352370,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No one dared tackle the 11\ncrossings until John Conway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356270,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He found all 552,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358910,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and claimed he did it\nin a single afternoon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361970,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was the last tabulation by hand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365060,
    "dDurationMs": 913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the '80s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365973,
    "dDurationMs": 2597,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dowker and Thistlethwaite\nbuilt a computer algorithm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368570,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to count all 12 and 13 crossing knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371840,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thistlethwaite later joined\nforces with Hoste and Weeks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374300,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tabulate all 14, 15\nand 16 crossing knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377930,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a paper titled \"The\nFirst 1,701,936 Knots.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383270,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The method they used is\nstill the one used today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386180,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employing a computer to\nlist all possible knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1388790,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then using invariants\nto weed out duplicates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391940,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They split into two teams\nand crosscheck their results,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395150,
    "dDurationMs": 3513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aligning perfectly on all but\nfour knots on their first try."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1400100,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2020, mathematician Ben Burton"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1402590,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single-handedly tabulated all\n17, 18 and 19 crossing knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407450,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bringing the total number\nof known prime knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409880,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 352,152,252."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415100,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His project was so\ncomputationally intensive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418010,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "several hundred computers\nhad to run for months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420410,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before obtaining the final number."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422960,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The hardest part of knot tabulation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425030,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is counting up every knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426890,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then carefully eliminating duplicates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429770,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you just want to generate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1431210,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a huge number of distinct knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1433100,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can make alternating knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435020,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knots with crossings that\nalternate over, under."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1437960,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This computation is much easier,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439760,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though it leaves out most knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1441950,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And back in 2007,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443330,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this method was used to\nfind alternating knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1445610,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up to an absurd 24 crossings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448640,
    "dDurationMs": 8513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in total, we know of\n159,965,097,353 knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457550,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, we're missing\na lot in between there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1461150,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory was always just pure math."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464000,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the algorithms,\ninvariants and tabulations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467060,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were knowledge for the sake of knowledge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1469670,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1989, chemist Jean-Pierre Sauvage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1472250,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tied molecules around copper ions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474350,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to form the first ever\nsynthetic knotted molecule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478160,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This trefoil knot restricted\nthe atoms from unfurling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481970,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trapping them in higher energy states"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483950,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to give the molecule new properties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486740,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any type of knot tied in a molecule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1488990,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will change its properties,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491060,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we know of over 159 billion knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1494780,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you can tie a molecule\ninto each of those knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497600,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's 159 billion new unique materials"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1501590,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "created from a single molecule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504260,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though after the trefoil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505430,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chemists have only managed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506510,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tie five other molecular knots to date."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509150,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a difficult task."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510290,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since they can't just nudge\nindividual ions into place,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1513740,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules must be built to\nself-assemble into knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517700,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory helps identify which knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519980,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "match available molecular templates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1522050,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "symmetric knots are easier for one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524150,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how to arrange those\nto assemble the knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529070,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most complex knot yet\ncreated is the 819 knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532880,
    "dDurationMs": 3753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with 192 atoms tied around\na central chloride ion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538670,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This molecule holds the\nGuinness World Record"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541250,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for tightest knot in the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543380,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "defined as the most\ncrossings per unit length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546080,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this case, eight\ncrossings in 20 nanometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549320,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since it's knotted around a chloride ion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551780,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once the ion is removed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1553580,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this molecule is one of the\nstrongest chloride binders"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556880,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1558350,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The field is still new\nfor specific applications."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1561830,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chemists are just focused\non creating molecular knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564500,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before thinking about\nmaterials development,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567110,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they hope to eventually build things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1568910,
    "dDurationMs": 3123,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like durable fabrics stronger than Kevlar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575060,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory is also critical\nto biological processes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578120,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that have saved millions of lives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1581690,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bacterial DNA consists of a single loop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1584480,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the double helix molecule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586430,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This shape means that it\nalways forms a knotted link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1589640,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it replicates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590960,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the bacteria can't\nseparate into two cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1593720,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with their DNA tangled up like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596060,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they have an enzyme called\ntype two topoisomerase,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1599390,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which snips and reconnects the DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This turns their linked\nDNA back into an unlink"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1606080,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they can replicate cleanly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608300,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you inhibit type two tophi summaries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1611150,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bacteria can't replicate properly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1613460,
    "dDurationMs": 1802,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in fact they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1615262,
    "dDurationMs": 3328,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is how some of the most\ncommon antibiotics in the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618590,
    "dDurationMs": 2292,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called quinolones operate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1620882,
    "dDurationMs": 2538,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Human DNA, while not circular,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1623420,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is long enough to also get into tangles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626420,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each cell in your body\ncontains two meters of DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629660,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the equivalent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1630560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of stuffing 200 kilometers of fishing line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633440,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a basketball."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1635300,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When this mess inevitably tangles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637670,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "human type two topoisomerases\ncome to make crossing changes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1642080,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The human version of the\nenzyme is different enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1644420,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the bacterial version"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645650,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it's unaffected by antibiotics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1648290,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But human topoisomerases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1650300,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are sometimes intentionally inhibited."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1653060,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This stops replication and kills cells,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1656450,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predominantly the rapidly\ndividing cancer cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659960,
    "dDurationMs": 3273,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's one of the most\ncommon forms of chemotherapy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1664640,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Biologists needed knot theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666590,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to first understand the mechanism\nof type two topoisomerase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1670850,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once they observed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671810,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was decreasing the crossing\nnumber of knots in DNA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674600,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two at a time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1676340,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they realized it had to\nbe cutting and rejoining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1678740,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire double strands of DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1681740,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are many other\nobscure topoisomerases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1684320,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that act on DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1685820,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory is used"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686780,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to analyze the knots they tie or untie"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689420,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how they operate as a result."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691820,
    "dDurationMs": 2063,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not just DNA that knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693883,
    "dDurationMs": 2917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1% of all proteins have various knots"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696800,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in their fundamental structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1698360,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they get misknotted, they malfunction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701300,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So being able to\naccurately tell knots apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1704210,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "helps understand these\nproteins' mechanisms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1706760,
    "dDurationMs": 3213,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as how to potentially\nrepair or utilize them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711500,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to your shoe laces,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1713480,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both of the common ways to tie the knot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1715400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are composed of two trefoils\non top of each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1718760,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm going to tie some rope around my leg"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1720950,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make this easier to see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723470,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you go counterclockwise\naround the loop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1727460,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then you form two identical trefoils"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1730640,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on top of each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1731720,
    "dDurationMs": 2405,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also known as a granny knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734125,
    "dDurationMs": 3895,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when you go clockwise around the loop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738020,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you get mirror imaged\ntrefoils on top of each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1742280,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is also known as a square knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744080,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it doesn't loosen as easily."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1746840,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we should all be tying\nour shoelaces like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750620,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clockwise around the loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753170,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of us aren't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1754003,
    "dDurationMs": 2167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, I'm not, usually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1756170,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I normally do it like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1758540,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A simple overhand knot\nis just the trefoil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1762080,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bow line knot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763160,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most common knot for boating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764630,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or just holding things\ntogether is the six two knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1768170,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And any knot tied without using the ends,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1770420,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also known as in the bite,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1772400,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is just an unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1775010,
    "dDurationMs": 3617,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a slipknot is an example of an unknot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2007, researchers Dorian\nRaymer and Douglas Smith"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786200,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "conducted 3,415 trials of\nspinning string in boxes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1791180,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to study how knots form in the real world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1797450,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They ended up creating 120\ndifferent types of knots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1801410,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some as complicated as 11 crossings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806090,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found that longer agitation time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1808160,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "led to a higher chance of knotting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1810170,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Longer string did as well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1812240,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except this probability decreased"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1814400,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once the string was put in a smaller box,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816530,
    "dDurationMs": 1593,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which restrained its motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1819170,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to keep\nsomething like headphones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1821300,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from knotting in your pocket"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822470,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you can't adjust string\nlength or agitation time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1825920,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then your best bet is to confine them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1827780,
    "dDurationMs": 2613,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to as small a space as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832600,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Raymer and Smith also proposed a model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1835160,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for real world knot formation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1837530,
    "dDurationMs": 1576,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A series of loops are first formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839106,
    "dDurationMs": 3974,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when a string is placed into a container."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1843080,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then when it's agitated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1844640,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a free end of the string"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1845930,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets woven up and down through the loops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1848360,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "braiding itself into them to form knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855470,
    "dDurationMs": 4743,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And let's see, a knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1861170,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So coiling up your wires"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1862940,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually setting\nyourself up for failure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1865280,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you're forming a bunch of loops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1867110,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a loose end to braid\nperfectly into a knot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1871040,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead, what you want to\ndo is restrict its movement,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1873710,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether by using a small box\nor increasing string stiffness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1877880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DNA increases its\nstiffness by super coiling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1880880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can do the same with your wires."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1883280,
    "dDurationMs": 2079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I just double it up like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1885359,
    "dDurationMs": 2991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then I twist from the middle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1888350,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is going to\nstiffen the length of wire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1892760,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is naturally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1893930,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going to want to sort of coil in on itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1896300,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's going to look\nlike a big tangled mess,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1898430,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but all you have to do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1899263,
    "dDurationMs": 4657,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is take the opposite ends of\nthe headphone and pull apart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1903920,
    "dDurationMs": 3243,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there's no tangles, no knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1909200,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their study won an Ig Nobel Prize."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1911450,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has been cited in studies\nof knots in surgical catheters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1914960,
    "dDurationMs": 4173,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even linked to an Apple\npatent for stiffer earbud wires."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1920630,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory began as a\nfailed theory of everything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1924350,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and for the next century,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1925460,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was a standalone field of math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1927620,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "propelled by nothing more\nthan intellectual curiosity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1931220,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in recent years, it's\nreclaimed its original potential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1935450,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, knot theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1936710,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a theory of everything\nfrom headphone tangles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1939920,
    "dDurationMs": 2643,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to material science to chemotherapy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1943400,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1889, Kelvin gave\na presidential address"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1946430,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the British Institution\nof Electrical Engineers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948650,
    "dDurationMs": 2827,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about his failed atomic theory of knots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1951477,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I am afraid I must end"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953037,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"by saying that the\ndifficulties are so great"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955257,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"in the way of forming anything\nlike a comprehensive theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958317,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"that we cannot even imagine a finger-post"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1960567,
    "dDurationMs": 3086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"pointing to a way that leads\nus towards the explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1964557,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"But this time next year,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1966177,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"this time 10 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1967857,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"this time 100 years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1969807,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I cannot doubt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1971007,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"but that these things which\nnow seem to us so mysterious"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1974337,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"will be no mysteries at all,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1976347,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"that the scales will fall from our eyes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1978897,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"that we shall learn to look\non things in a different way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1982197,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"when that which is now a difficulty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1984027,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"will be the only common sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1985977,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"and intelligible way of\nlooking at the subject.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1995930,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knot theory is a perfect example"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1997730,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how knowledge in one area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1999230,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can become a tool to\nunderstand countless others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2002080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From learning how to tell a\ntrefoil apart from an unknot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2005680,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knot theorists have built all the way up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2007480,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to discovering brand new proteins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2009910,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want a quick and easy way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2011410,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to build out your own mental toolkit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2013240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should absolutely check\nout this video sponsor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2015640,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brilliant.org."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2017230,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant is the best way to\nlearn about almost any concept"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2020320,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in math, data science,\nprogramming and more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2023110,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They even have a\ncomputational biology course"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025360,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you can apply\nconcepts from this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2027760,
    "dDurationMs": 1943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to folding protein chains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2029703,
    "dDurationMs": 2587,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Brilliant, you just set your goal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2032290,
    "dDurationMs": 2164,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they'll design the\nperfect learning path"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2034454,
    "dDurationMs": 1196,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to help you reach it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2035650,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "equipping you with professional\ntools along the way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2038800,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Want to harness the tools\nof a data scientist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2041440,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant's newest course\nPredicting with Probability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2044020,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the best place to get them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2045970,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The course has everything you\nneed and nothing you don't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2049330,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to start building your\ndata science skills."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2052150,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no coding required."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2054220,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll learn easily to slice\nand dice massive data sets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2057940,
